KDOS icon theme — attribution and deviations
============================================

This theme is a derivative work of the Papirus icon theme.

    Upstream:  https://github.com/PapirusDevelopmentTeam/papirus-icon-theme
    License:   GNU General Public License, version 3
    Vendored:  see art/UPSTREAM for the exact release
    Full text: art/LICENSE.upstream (installed as LICENSE.papirus)

Papirus is itself based on the Paper icon set by Sam Hewitt.

This derivative is distributed under the same licence, GPL-3.0. The complete
corresponding source is the contents of art/ (the pruned upstream artwork,
otherwise unmodified) together with vendor.py and kdos-theme (src/packages/kdos-theme/icons.c), which are the
only things that produce the installed files.

What KDOS changed
-----------------

1. apps/ is not vendored at all. The alien apps ship their own icons and
   script/06_packaging/01_appbox.sh installs them into the system hicolor
   tree; replacing Firefox's and GIMP's own marks with redraws makes the
   launcher harder to read, not easier. It is also 76 MB of the 90.

2. Only six sizes are kept (16, 22, 24, 32, 48, 64). Upstream ships 8 through
   128 plus an @2x alias for each.

3. Only the default folder/user colourway (blue) is kept. Upstream ships
   twenty-two, none of which KDOS exposes any way to select, and blue is the
   one the unsuffixed names already alias to.

4. Papirus-Dark is merged over Papirus into a single theme rather than kept as
   a second one: it differs only at 16/22/24 and symlinks back to Papirus for
   everything else, and KDOS has no light mode.

5. Aliases are preserved as symlinks. Any alias left dangling by the pruning
   above is dropped.

6. Every colour in every remaining SVG is remapped to the KDOS palette by
   kdos-theme icons: hues are mapped by family (blue/green/purple to the accent,
   yellow/orange/brown to the secondary, red to the urgent colour, near-greys
   to a faintly tinted neutral) with each icon's own lightness and saturation
   preserved. Papirus colour-codes mimetypes, and that coding survives — a PDF
   stays red and an audio file stays amber — while folders, devices and places
   become phosphor.

7. index.theme is replaced: the theme is named KDOS and inherits Cosmic, Pop
   and hicolor so COSMIC's own applet icons and the alien apps' icons still
   resolve.

No upstream path, geometry or shape is otherwise altered.
